 "_about": "EarFun's control protocols (docs/earfun/PROTOCOL.md), read from EarFun's own app (EarFun Audio 20.1.61, com.corelink.earfun, decompiled outside the repo on 2026-11-03; none of its code is here): device/protocol/headset (QualcommProtocolParser and its TW600, TW700 and HP1000 subclasses, EarfunProtocolParser and its CW100 subclass, and the inline subclasses in device/base/DeviceType). Both run over the standard serial port. 'qualcomm' is GAIA v2 with vendor 000A, as SOUNDPEATS' Qualcomm models speak it: a command is 03xx and its answer 83xx or 03xx, the value at the answer's fourth byte. 'earfun' is EarFun's own frame: EF, the command (two bytes), the payload's length, the payload, (length + sum of the payload) & FF, FE. never_send marks factory reset, renaming, firmware update and device management; confirm marks restarting and powering off, which PairFree sends only from an action the user confirms on screen (owner, 2026-11-03); private marks reads that return phones' names and addresses or a serial number, which PairFree never sends.",
